罐子在爆炸。

1028
00:52:26.720 --> 00:52:29.040
We got a fan question about that as well.
我们收到了关于这一幕的一个粉丝提问。

1029
00:52:29.840 --> 00:52:30.220
John D.
来自科罗拉多州莱克伍德的约翰·D

1030
00:52:30.360 --> 00:52:32.960
from Lakewood, Colorado said, how did they do that?
问道，他们是怎么做到的？

1031
00:52:33.320 --> 00:52:34.120
Was it real?
那是真的吗？

1032
00:52:34.260 --> 00:52:35.240
Was it special effects?
是特效吗？

1033
00:52:35.640 --> 00:52:37.240
I mean, the cans were real.
我是说，罐子确实是真的。

1034
00:52:37.540 --> 00:52:40.620
I guess this gag drove the crew crazy.
我猜这个恶作剧把剧组人员折腾疯了。

1035
00:52:40.880 --> 00:52:45.100
Randy, Kelly, and Veda shared that it was just a very difficult thing to get.
兰迪、凯利和维达分享说，这其实是个很难拍出来的效果。

1036
00:52:45.200 --> 00:52:47.520
It seems like a small little moment, right, in the script?
在剧本里这似乎只是个微不足道的小片段，对吧？

1037
00:52:47.520 --> 00:52:49.400
But it was very hard to capture.
但要捕捉到这个画面非常困难。

1038
00:52:50.280 --> 00:52:50.420
Yeah.
是的。

1039
00:52:50.760 --> 00:52:57.360
Randy told me that the writers were so tickled by this idea that these cans would explode.
兰迪告诉我，编剧们对这些罐子会爆炸这个点子感到十分好笑。

1040
00:52:57.600 --> 00:53:00.240
That Michael would put full cans, you guys.
迈克尔放的竟然是整罐的汽水，各位。

1041
00:53:00.340 --> 00:53:01.860
You're supposed to put empty cans.
按理说你们应该放空罐子。

1042
00:53:02.040 --> 00:53:02.180
Yes.
没错。

1043
00:53:02.260 --> 00:53:03.700
But Michael wouldn't think that through.
但迈克尔可不会考虑得那么周全。

1044
00:53:04.020 --> 00:53:10.820
They started by just dragging some full cans behind the car, hoping they would explode.
他们一开始只是在车后拖了几个满罐，希望它们能自己炸开。

1045
00:53:10.820 --> 00:53:11.820
They didn't.
结果并没有。

1046
00:53:11.820 --> 00:53:20.060
So they actually had to rig each can with a teeny tiny timed explosive charge to make them burst open.
所以他们实际上不得不在每个罐子上都装上一个微型定时爆炸装置，才能让它们破裂开来。

1047
00:53:20.680 --> 00:53:21.660
That happened.
确实是这么做的。

1048
00:53:21.780 --> 00:53:24.140
They burst open, but it wasn't all that exciting.
它们确实炸开了，但看起来并没有那么刺激。

1049
00:53:24.140 --> 00:53:29.680
So then they also had to add like a sound effect to make it sort of louder.
所以他们后来还得加上音效，好让声音显得更大一些。

1050
00:53:29.960 --> 00:53:33.460
It was a very difficult little bit to pull off.
这真是一个很难完成的小笑料。

1051
00:53:34.220 --> 00:53:38.160
But listen, this is a tradition, the thing of putting cans on the back of your car.
但听我说，这是一个传统，就是在车后面绑易拉罐的做法。

1052
00:53:38.160 --> 00:53:40.000
Of course, I looked it up.
当然，我查过了。

1053
00:53:40.140 --> 00:53:45.360
I guess that this goes all the way back to a French tradition, Angela.
我猜这可以追溯到一个法国传统，安吉拉。

1054
00:53:45.680 --> 00:53:46.020
Oh.
哦。

1055
00:53:46.260 --> 00:53:50.620
It's called, I'm going to pronounce this wrong, chivalry.
它被称为——我可能会读错——charivari（闹婚）。

1056
00:53:52.060 --> 00:53:58.180
And you're supposed to like create a bunch of noise after a couple is newly married.
人们本意是在新婚夫妇新婚后制造出一堆噪音。

1057
00:53:58.800 --> 00:54:06.260
It was originally done where, as the couple drove away, people would clang pots and pans and other noisemakers.
最初的做法是，当新人开车离开时，大家会敲击锅碗瓢盆和其他噪音制造器。

1058
00:54:06.560 --> 00:54:09.120
But then it eventually evolved into the can thing.
但后来它最终演变成了绑易拉罐的做法。

1059
00:54:09.680 --> 00:54:11.840
But I thought you'd like this one, Angela.
不过我想你会喜欢这个的，安吉拉。

1060
00:54:12.140 --> 00:54:12.620
Okay.
好的。

1061
00:54:12.620 --> 00:54:15.220
I guess in the Tudor period in England.
我猜是在英国的都铎时期。

1062
00:54:15.340 --> 00:54:18.360
I was going to say, how far back does this go?
我正想问，这能追溯到多久以前？

1063
00:54:18.360 --> 00:54:19.020
Yeah.
是啊。

1064
00:54:19.300 --> 00:54:29.520
There was this crazy tradition where as the couple would ride away in their carriage, guests would take off their shoes and throw them at the carriage.
当时有一个疯狂的传统，当新人坐着马车离开时，客人们会脱下鞋子朝马车扔去。

1065
00:54:30.300 --> 00:54:33.080
And if you hit the carriage, it meant good luck.
如果你砸中了马车，就意味着好运。

1066
00:54:33.300 --> 00:54:38.920
So there have always been these little traditions of things to do as a couple is driving away.
所以一直以来都有这些小传统，在新婚夫妇开车离开时要做点什么。

1067
00:54:39.420 --> 00:54:41.140
Throwing things at them.
向他们扔东西。

1068
00:54:41.420 --> 00:54:42.440
Clanking noise.
制造敲击的噪音。

1069
00:54:43.020 --> 00:54:43.180
Yeah.
是啊。

1070
00:54:44.320 --> 00:54:47.380
But that stunt was a nightmare.
但那个特技简直是噩梦。

1071
00:54:48.460 --> 00:54:50.580
I have a driving stunt coming up.
我接下来还有一个驾驶特技。

1072
00:54:50.860 --> 00:54:51.720
Yes, you do.
没错，你确实有。

1073
00:54:52.000 --> 00:54:53.280
You're going to run into Kevin.
你要撞上凯文了。

1074
00:54:54.800 --> 00:54:58.020
I fully nudge Brian Baumgartner with that car, you guys.
伙计们，我真的用那辆车轻轻撞了布莱恩·鲍姆加特纳一下。

1075
00:54:58.200 --> 00:54:59.440
And it was a lot of fun.
而且这真的很有趣。

1076
00:54:59.620 --> 00:55:02.960
Listen, I was going 0.000 miles an hour.
听着，我当时的时速是0.000英里。

1077
00:55:03.100 --> 00:55:03.780
It's just a little tap.
这只是轻轻碰了一下。

1078
00:55:03.900 --> 00:55:04.540
Just a little tap.
只是轻轻碰了一下。

1079
00:55:04.900 --> 00:55:06.980
And we actually had a lot of fun doing that.
我们拍的时候其实觉得挺好玩的。

1080
00:55:07.100 --> 00:55:08.000
I got really tickled.
我当时真的乐不可支。

1081
00:55:09.080 --> 00:55:10.620
Everyone's on their way to Niagara now.
大家都已经在去尼亚加拉的路上。

1082
00:55:10.780 --> 00:55:12.420
You have all these different pairings and cars.
你会看到各种不同的组合和车辆。

1083
00:55:12.420 --> 00:55:13.400
It's really fun to see.
看着真的很有趣。

1084
00:55:13.540 --> 00:55:14.940
You have Andy, Aaron, and Kelly.
有安迪、埃伦和凯莉。

1085
00:55:15.340 --> 00:55:16.760
And you have Jim and Pam.
还有吉姆和帕姆。

1086
00:55:16.760 --> 00:55:18.240
Pam and Michael and Dwight.
帕姆、迈克尔和德怀特。

1087
00:55:18.740 --> 00:55:19.020
Yes.
没错。

1088
00:55:19.360 --> 00:55:22.160
There's that super sweet scene with Pam and Jim.
帕姆和吉姆有那个超级温馨的场景。

1089
00:55:22.380 --> 00:55:25.960
And this is where we get, oh my gosh, I just loved it.
这就是我们迎来——天哪，我太喜欢了。

1090
00:55:26.460 --> 00:55:32.920
Pam tells Jim that her aunt told her to take mental pictures of the high points of their wedding day
帕姆告诉吉姆，她阿姨让她把婚礼当天的精彩时刻拍成“心灵照片”留作纪念

1091
00:55:32.920 --> 00:55:36.420
because everything's going to go by so fast and they should try to remember it.
因为一切都会过得飞快，他们应该试着记住它。

1092
00:55:36.420 --> 00:55:41.720
And that's when Jim uses his fingers and pretends like he's taking a picture of Pam.
然后吉姆就用手指假装在给帕姆拍照。

1093
00:55:41.720 --> 00:55:46.920
Pam, this idea that Jim and Pam should take mental pictures was a pitch from Steve Carell.
帕姆，吉姆和帕姆应该拍“心灵照片”这个点子是史蒂夫·卡瑞尔提出的。

1094
00:55:47.120 --> 00:55:52.260
He had told Greg this story that he had a friend who would do this.
他曾向格雷格讲过这样一个故事，说他有个朋友会这么做。

1095
00:55:52.420 --> 00:55:55.760
And so Greg put it into the script for Jim and Pam.
于是格雷格把它写进了吉姆和帕姆的剧本里。

1096
00:55:55.760 --> 00:55:59.960
But when we read it, John and I, we didn't get it like when we read the script.
但当我们读到它时，我和约翰在读剧本时并没有领会到它的意思。

1097
00:56:00.580 --> 00:56:03.300
So Greg did that thing where he was like, Steve, come here, come here.
所以格雷格就做出了那种举动，他说：“史蒂夫，过来，过来。”

1098
00:56:03.540 --> 00:56:04.740
Show these guys what you meant.
“给这俩人演示一下你是什么意思。”

1099
00:56:04.860 --> 00:56:06.460
The thing with the taking the mental pictures.
就是拍“心灵照片”那个事。

1100
00:56:06.700 --> 00:56:08.420
So Steve kind of showed us.
于是史蒂夫就给我们示范了一下。

1101
00:56:08.860 --> 00:56:11.280
And then we were like, oh, we get it.
然后我们就觉得，哦，我们懂了。

1102
00:56:11.280 --> 00:56:12.860
I just love that so much.
我真的太喜欢这个了。

1103
00:56:12.940 --> 00:56:17.260
And it goes to what Greg mentioned in the commentary, you guys, and also in our interview
这呼应了格雷格在评论音轨里提到的话，各位，还有我们的采访

1104
00:56:17.720 --> 00:56:22.920
about how a lot of this episode was based off real life moments in people's lives.
关于这一集有很多内容都是基于人们生活中的真实瞬间。

1105
00:56:23.080 --> 00:56:23.900
And this is one of them.
而这就是其中之一。

1106
00:56:24.080 --> 00:56:27.020
You know, I also improvised a line in the scene, Angela.
你知道吗，我在这个场景里也即兴发挥了一句台词，安吉拉。

1107
00:56:27.300 --> 00:56:27.940
Which line?
哪一句？

1108
00:56:29.620 --> 00:56:34.420
When Jim says, oh, you blinked, that was supposed to be the end.
当吉姆说，哦，你眨眼了，本来这应该就结束了。

1109
00:56:34.840 --> 00:56:39.560
And I improvised the line, oh, we should have hired a professional to take our mental pictures.
然后我即兴加了一句，哦，我们真该请个专业人士来拍我们的脑海照片。

1110
00:56:39.920 --> 00:56:40.340
Aw.
噢。

1111
00:56:41.040 --> 00:56:42.160
I'm very proud of it.
我对此感到非常骄傲。

1112
00:56:42.280 --> 00:56:43.320
It's very good.
这非常不错。

1113
00:56:44.160 --> 00:56:47.740
So Angela, you mentioned that Dwight and Michael are in the car together.
那么安吉拉，你提到德怀特和迈克尔一起坐在车里。

1114
00:56:47.780 --> 00:56:54.400
And I laughed out loud so hard at the beginning of the scene when you find out that Michael
当这一幕开始，你发现迈克尔

1115
00:56:54.400 --> 00:56:56.900
is asleep and driving.
在睡着的同时还在开车时，我简直笑出了声。

1116
00:56:57.360 --> 00:56:57.760
Yeah.
是啊。

1117
00:56:58.160 --> 00:56:59.640
It was so funny.
太搞笑了。

1118
00:56:59.880 --> 00:57:07.540
I also laughed out loud when Dwight says he made Michael a mix CD, something he can play
当德怀特说他给迈克尔制作了一张精选CD，如果迈克尔

1119
00:57:07.540 --> 00:57:09.680
if he brings a woman back to his room.
带女人回他的房间就可以播放时，我也笑出了声。

1120
00:57:09.680 --> 00:57:12.120
I mean, Dwight is a wingman, guys.
我的意思是，德怀特真是个僚机，各位。

1121
00:57:12.520 --> 00:57:14.480
I loved it so much.
我太喜欢了。

1122
00:57:14.480 --> 00:57:16.260
I felt like we needed to hear it.
我觉得我们必须听听看。

1123
00:57:17.480 --> 00:57:17.660
Hello.
你好。

1124
00:57:18.180 --> 00:57:19.660
My name is Dwight Schrute.
我叫德怀特·舒鲁特。

1125
00:57:19.900 --> 00:57:24.100
If you are listening to this, you're a lucky woman Michael has seduced.
如果你正在听这个，说明你是个被迈克尔诱惑的幸运女人。

1126
00:57:24.280 --> 00:57:26.160
Ah, to be in your shoes.
啊，真羡慕你。

1127
00:57:26.540 --> 00:57:27.400
What's next?
接下来是什么？

1128
00:57:27.400 --> 00:57:28.540
You're probably wondering.
你可能在纳闷。

1129
00:57:28.860 --> 00:57:31.460
Don't be scared of your night in heaven.
不要害怕你在天堂般的夜晚。

1130
00:57:33.710 --> 00:57:36.890
I mean, it's so creepy.
我的意思是，这太诡异了。

1131
00:57:37.690 --> 00:57:39.090
Maximum creep factor.
诡异程度拉满。

1132
00:57:39.730 --> 00:57:43.010
This scene made me laugh for something I was not expecting, Jenna.
这个场景让我笑是因为一些我没料到的事，珍娜。

1133
00:57:43.630 --> 00:57:44.090
What?
什么？

1134
00:57:45.310 --> 00:57:47.790
I couldn't stop cracking up.
我忍不住一直狂笑。

1135
00:57:47.990 --> 00:57:48.610
I don't know why.
我不知道为什么。

1136
00:57:48.750 --> 00:57:50.110
Maybe I was just in a loopy mood.
也许我当时脑子有点犯晕。

1137
00:57:50.390 --> 00:57:55.690
I don't know if it was intentional or not, but did you notice that Michael is dressed just
我不知道这算不算刻意安排，但你有没有注意到迈克尔的穿着

1138
00:57:55.690 --> 00:57:56.770
like his car seat?
和他的车座一模一样？

1139
00:57:57.150 --> 00:57:57.590
What?
什么？

1140
00:57:57.870 --> 00:58:00.970
He's dressed exactly like the upholstery in his car.
他的穿着和车里的内饰简直一模一样。

1141
00:58:01.310 --> 00:58:07.170
So he's in all beige and the seat is all beige and he's just like a beige blob going down
所以他全身都是米色，座椅也全都是米色，他就好像一团米色色块在路上

1142
00:58:07.170 --> 00:58:09.770
the road and it just cracked me up.
行驶，这真的把我逗乐了。

1143
00:58:10.070 --> 00:58:12.750
I did not, but I want to go back and look at it.
我没有注意到，但我得回去看看。

1144
00:58:13.170 --> 00:58:16.310
Well, you guys, the gang finally makes it to Niagara.
好了，各位，大家终于抵达了尼亚加拉。

1145
00:58:16.530 --> 00:58:17.810
They're pulling into the city.
他们正驶入这座城市。

1146
00:58:18.070 --> 00:58:22.790
For that driving sequence as everyone arrives to Niagara, Kelly Cantley shared,
关于大家抵达尼亚加拉的那段驾驶戏，凯莉·坎特利分享说，

1147
00:58:22.970 --> 00:58:27.110
that was filmed, Jenna, while you guys were drying off from Maid of the MiSt.
珍娜，那是你们从“雾中少女号”游船上来、身上还没干的时候拍的。

1148
00:58:27.590 --> 00:58:28.590
Oh, wow.
哦，哇。

1149
00:58:28.790 --> 00:58:29.090
Yeah.
是啊。

1150
00:58:29.550 --> 00:58:37.010
For the most part, we shot this episode in Los Angeles and all of the scenes at the hotel
大部分情况下，我们这一集是在洛杉矶拍摄的，所有的酒店场景也是

1151
00:58:37.170 --> 00:58:40.870
were shot at Sportsman's Lodge in Studio City.
是在工作室城的体育俱乐部小屋拍摄的。

1152
00:58:41.810 --> 00:58:47.110
For the lobby area, we used an area that was under renovation that was kind of in the back
对于大堂区域，我们使用了一个正在翻修的区域，它有点在

1153
00:58:47.110 --> 00:58:47.710
of the hotel.
酒店的后面。

1154
00:58:48.210 --> 00:58:53.690
Our production designer, Michael Gallenberg, and our set decorator, Steve Rothstein, they
我们的制作设计师迈克尔·加伦伯格和我们的布景师史蒂夫·罗斯斯坦，他们

1155
00:58:53.690 --> 00:59:00.210
basically turned this unused lobby into this fictitious Statler Falls Hotel.
基本上把这个未使用的的大堂变成了虚构的斯塔特勒福尔斯酒店。

1156
00:59:00.710 --> 00:59:02.190
What an amazing job.
真是太了不起了。

1157
00:59:02.390 --> 00:59:06.330
I mean, everything from like the fireplace, all of it that you see, they put in there.
我的意思是，从壁炉开始的一切，你看到的所有的东西，都是他们放进去的。

1158
00:59:06.330 --> 00:59:11.530
Everything, all the hotel rooms, they were upstairs on the second floor.
所有的东西，所有的酒店房间，都在二楼。

1159
00:59:11.710 --> 00:59:15.630
It was an unused wing of the hotel that was undergoing a renovation at the time.
那是酒店的一个闲置侧翼，当时正在进行翻修。

1160
00:59:15.850 --> 00:59:16.870
They were empty.
它们都是空的。

1161
00:59:17.150 --> 00:59:22.830
So literally everything you see was added by our design crews, which I just think is amazing.
所以从字面上看，你看到的每一样东西都是我们的设计团队添加的，我觉得这太棒了。

1162
00:59:23.630 --> 00:59:29.730
And lady, do you remember when we talked to Ed Helms about when he started on the office,
而且，女士，你还记得我们跟艾德·海尔姆斯聊过他刚进《办公室》的时候吗，

1163
00:59:29.730 --> 00:59:33.130
he stayed at Sportsman's Lodge?
他住在体育俱乐部小屋？

1164
00:59:33.610 --> 00:59:34.810
Yeah, that's where they put him up.
对，那是他们给他安排的地方。

1165
00:59:35.070 --> 00:59:35.590
Yes.
是的。

1166
00:59:36.850 --> 00:59:42.490
Incidentally, when Lee and I got married, Sportsman's Lodge was down the street from our house.
顺便说一句，当我和李结婚时，体育俱乐部小屋就在我们家附近的一条街上。

1167
00:59:43.030 --> 00:59:47.290
And we found out that you could buy a day pass for their swimming pool.
我们发现你可以买他们游泳池的日票。

1168
00:59:47.450 --> 00:59:51.190
They have a huge swimming pool, like an Olympic-sized swimming pool.
他们有一个巨大的游泳池，就像奥运会标准大小的游泳池一样。

1169
00:59:51.190 --> 00:59:58.270
And so whenever my family would come to town, we would get day passes for the Sportsman's Lodge swimming pool.
所以每当我的家人来到镇上，我们就会买体育俱乐部小屋游泳池的日票。

1170
00:59:58.710 --> 01:00:01.190
Jenna, my dad loved the Sportsman's Lodge.
珍娜，我爸爸很喜欢体育俱乐部小屋。

1171
01:00:01.670 --> 01:00:04.070
We would go there and swim and hang out.
我们会去那里游泳和闲逛。

1172
01:00:04.150 --> 01:00:08.270
And you and I often met there for breakfast because they had a fantastic breakfaSt.
而且你和我经常在那里碰面吃早餐，因为他们的早餐棒极了。

1173
01:00:08.610 --> 01:00:11.730
They had an amazing little breakfast diner restaurant thing.
他们有一个神奇的小型早餐餐馆之类的东西。

1174
01:00:11.730 --> 01:00:19.810
Well, Randy also shared with me that we had to do a table read for one of our upcoming episodes while we were shooting at Sportsman's Lodge.
嗯，兰迪还跟我分享说，我们在体育俱乐部小屋拍摄时，必须为我们即将到来的一集进行剧本围读。

1175
01:00:19.970 --> 01:00:26.670
And they put us in this conference room, but it had a huge window right onto the swimming pool.
他们把我们安排在这个会议室里，但它有一个正对游泳池的大窗户。

1176
01:00:26.830 --> 01:00:28.770
He said we got a lot of looky-loos.
他说我们吸引了很多好奇的观众。

1177
01:00:28.910 --> 01:00:35.090
A lot of people like in their bathing suits and towels just like walking by watching us read an episode of The Office.
很多人穿着泳衣，拿着毛巾，从旁边走过，看着我们围读《办公室》的一集。

1178
01:00:35.090 --> 01:00:44.090
Also, try concentrating on reading and delivering a line as like some guy is chasing after a beach ball in his swim trunks.
另外，当某个穿着泳裤的家伙在追着沙滩球跑时，还要集中精力阅读和台词表达，这可真难。

1179
01:00:44.410 --> 01:00:47.550
Well, now Jim and Pam are going to check in to their hotel room.
好了，现在吉姆和帕姆要去登记入住他们的酒店房间了。

1180
01:00:47.910 --> 01:00:51.810
And I want you guys to look at 8 minutes, 41 seconds.
我想让你们看看8分41秒处。

1181
01:00:52.450 --> 01:00:59.510
There is a beautiful photo, a huge picture in the lobby of Niagara Falls, of the actual falls.
大堂里有一张美丽的照片，一张巨大的尼亚加拉大瀑布的照片，也就是真正的瀑布。

1182
01:00:59.790 --> 01:01:03.050
Well, that was taken by our very own Michael Gallenberg.
嗯，那是我们自己的迈克尔·加伦伯格拍的。

1183
01:01:03.050 --> 01:01:05.350
Randy and Michael had gone there to scout.
兰迪和迈克尔去那里勘景了。

1184
01:01:05.590 --> 01:01:11.070
And on their scouting trip, Michael took that picture and blew it up really big and made it part of the lobby decoration.
在他们的勘景之旅中，迈克尔拍下了那张照片，并把它放得很大，成了大堂装饰的一部分。

1185
01:01:11.630 --> 01:01:13.110
Oh, I love that detail.
哦，我喜欢这个细节。

1186
01:01:13.530 --> 01:01:17.690
During this scene, Jim and Pam make it clear that they're going to get individual rooms tonight.
在这个场景中，吉姆和帕姆明确表示他们今晚要住单人间。

1187
01:01:17.770 --> 01:01:20.710
And then the next night, they're going to check into the honeymoon suite.
然后第二天晚上，他们要入住蜜月套房。

1188
01:01:20.930 --> 01:01:23.450
But they're wondering, like, can we just take a peek at it?
但他们在想，呃，我们能先看一眼吗？

1189
01:01:23.530 --> 01:01:24.670
We just want to look at it.
我们只是想看一眼。

1190
01:01:24.990 --> 01:01:27.810
And the hotel desk clerk is like, oh, I'm sorry.
酒店前台接待员说，哦，我很抱歉。

1191
01:01:28.150 --> 01:01:29.650
Someone has that room tonight.
今晚有人住那个房间了。

1192
01:01:30.050 --> 01:01:31.610
And that someone is Andy.
而那个人就是安迪。

1193
01:01:33.050 --> 01:01:34.770
He's staying in the honeymoon suite.
他住在蜜月套房里。

1194
01:01:34.990 --> 01:01:36.230
The night before.
在前一天晚上。

1195
01:01:36.470 --> 01:01:38.570
And he's like, I'll break it in for you guys.
他说，我来为你们试用一下。

1196
01:01:39.230 --> 01:01:40.430
John delivers this line.
约翰说出了这句台词。

1197
01:01:40.510 --> 01:01:41.310
It was in the script.
剧本里是这么写的。

1198
01:01:41.490 --> 01:01:43.890
I had to look it up because the way he did it was so funny.
我不得不去查一下，因为他演得太搞笑了。

1199
01:01:43.970 --> 01:01:45.910
I thought maybe he made it up on the fly.
我还以为他是即兴发挥的呢。

1200
01:01:46.150 --> 01:01:48.590
He just says, I do not like that.
他只是说，我可不喜欢这样。

1201
01:01:50.010 --> 01:01:51.090
I do not like that.
我可不喜欢那样。

1202
01:01:51.490 --> 01:01:52.530
It's so great.
这太棒了。

1203
01:01:53.190 --> 01:01:57.170
Well, listen, I have a guest star alert that is near and dear to my heart.
听着，我有一个特别嘉宾的预告，这对我来说意义非凡。

1204
01:01:57.170 --> 01:02:03.910
The woman who plays the front desk clerk throughout this episode is my friend, Michelle Gunn.
在这集里扮演前台接待员的女士是我的朋友米歇尔·冈恩。

1205
01:02:04.330 --> 01:02:07.150
Now, I have known Michelle for so long.
我和米歇尔认识很久了。

1206
01:02:07.150 --> 01:02:14.810
And she auditioned for The Office six times for six different roles before landing this one.
她在拿到这个角色之前，为了六个不同的角色为《办公室》试镜了六次。

1207
01:02:15.030 --> 01:02:15.950
I didn't know that.
我不知道这件事。

1208
01:02:15.950 --> 01:02:21.550
Yes, and she would get to the final callbacks and then they'd give the role to someone else.
对啊，她每次都进了最终复试，然后他们就把角色给了别人。

1209
01:02:21.690 --> 01:02:23.830
But Allison Jones kept bringing her back.
但艾莉森·琼斯一直让她回来试镜。

1210
01:02:24.070 --> 01:02:27.170
We would always be so bummed when she didn't get a role.
每当她没拿到角色时，我们总是感到非常沮丧。

1211
01:02:27.450 --> 01:02:33.090
But then she got this huge role where she got to interact with almost every cast member.
但后来她得到了这个重要的角色，有机会与几乎每一位演员演对手戏。

1212
01:02:33.330 --> 01:02:35.630
She got to be directed by Paul Feig.
她还得到了保罗·费格的执导。

1213
01:02:35.630 --> 01:02:39.550
And she got paid for two different episodes.
而且她拿了两集的薪水。

1214
01:02:39.910 --> 01:02:41.490
So we were so excited.
所以我们都超级兴奋。

1215
01:02:41.630 --> 01:02:49.890
We were like, oh my gosh, this is that story where like every job you didn't get leads to the job you absolutely were meant to have.
我们当时想，天哪，这就是那种你没得到的工作最终都会指引你走向命中注定的那份工作的故事。

1216
01:02:50.030 --> 01:02:51.130
How fun.
多有意思啊。

1217
01:02:51.430 --> 01:02:52.830
And she's so good in it.
而且她在里面的表现太棒了。

1218
01:02:52.910 --> 01:02:53.810
She's so good.
她演得太好了。

1219
01:02:54.030 --> 01:02:54.990
Oh, she crushed it.
哦，她演得太绝了。

1220
01:02:55.190 --> 01:02:59.410
I want you to know, I noticed a background catch in this scene, Angela.
安吉拉，我想让你知道，我在这个场景里发现了一个背景里的细节。

1221
01:02:59.690 --> 01:03:00.950
It's really quick.
非常快。

1222
01:03:01.170 --> 01:03:01.710
What'd you got?
你发现了什么？

1223
01:03:01.710 --> 01:03:12.070
Okay, there is like a little announcement board that sort of says all the other things that are happening at the hotel on this night.
好啦，这里好像有一个小公告板，上面写着这天晚上酒店里还将举办的其他各种活动。

1224
01:03:12.290 --> 01:03:13.210
Oh, what's it say?
哦，上面写了什么？

1225
01:03:13.570 --> 01:03:14.070
All right.
好吧。

1226
01:03:14.350 --> 01:03:17.390
I live for this, by the way, and I'm sad I missed it.
顺便说一句，我最爱看这些了，没能亲自发现让我很难过。

1227
01:03:17.490 --> 01:03:18.730
So I cannot wait to hear.
所以我等不及要听了。

1228
01:03:19.070 --> 01:03:26.710
Well, in addition to Jim and Pam's rehearsal dinner, you could also attend the Moose Lodge meeting at 7 p.m.
嗯，除了吉姆和帕姆的彩排晚宴，你还可以在晚上7点去麋鹿厅参加驼鹿小屋会议。

1229
01:03:26.810 --> 01:03:27.510
in the Elk Room.
在麋鹿厅。

1230
01:03:28.770 --> 01:03:32.450
Or Senior Poker Friday at 5 p.m.
或者下午5点在河景厅参加老年扑克周五活动。

1231
01:03:32.570 --> 01:03:33.450
in the River Room.
在河景厅。

1232
01:03:33.970 --> 01:03:38.670
Or perhaps you'd like to go to the O'Brien Retirement Party at 8 p.m.
或者你可能想在晚上8点去接待大厅参加奥布莱恩退休派对。

1233
01:03:38.670 --> 01:03:40.330
in the Reception Hall.
在接待大厅。

1234
01:03:41.230 --> 01:03:43.350
I also noticed this tidbit.
我还注意到了这个有趣的小花絮。

1235
01:03:43.750 --> 01:03:48.910
I know exactly when Jim and Pam's wedding reception is because it's on the board.
我确切地知道吉姆和帕姆的婚礼招待会在什么时候，因为牌子上写着。

1236
01:03:48.910 --> 01:03:50.370
It's 2 p.m.
是下午2点。

1237
01:03:50.650 --> 01:03:52.630
the next day in the Falls Room.
第二天在瀑布厅。

1238
01:03:52.630 --> 01:03:55.890
So they had like, I guess, like a noon-ish wedding.
所以我想他们的婚礼大概是在中午左右吧。

1239
01:03:56.630 --> 01:04:00.130
Well, someone's going to get some bad news when they try to check into the hotel,
好吧，当有人试图登记入住酒店时，注定会听到一个坏消息，

1240
01:04:00.130 --> 01:04:07.730
and that person is Michael because I guess he thought you could just show up and say you want a room with the Beasley-Halpert block.
那个人就是迈克尔，因为我猜他以为只要现身说自己想要一间比斯利-哈尔珀特预留房就行了。

1241
01:04:08.050 --> 01:04:09.430
And you would have a room.
然后就能拿到一间房。

1242
01:04:09.810 --> 01:04:11.270
That's not how it works.
事情可不是这样的。

1243
01:04:11.450 --> 01:04:12.050
Oh, Michael.
哦，迈克尔。

1244
01:04:12.650 --> 01:04:16.650
So Michael's going to try to weasel himself into other people's rooMs.
所以迈克尔打算死皮赖脸地挤进别人的房间。

1245
01:04:16.990 --> 01:04:19.250
Of course no one wants Michael in their room.
当然没有人想让迈克尔进他们的房间。

1246
01:04:19.430 --> 01:04:23.890
The only person who's nice enough to say, Michael, you could have the other bed, is Toby.
唯一一个心好到说“迈克尔，你可以睡另一张床”的人是托比。

1247
01:04:24.190 --> 01:04:26.170
And Michael's like, um, hell no, Toby.
而迈克尔的反应是，呃，见鬼去吧，托比。

1248
01:04:26.670 --> 01:04:27.670
I know.
我懂的。

1249
01:04:28.350 --> 01:04:33.250
You know, Stanley's going to arrive to check in with not his wife.
你知道的，斯坦利登记入住时带的不是他的妻子。

1250
01:04:33.730 --> 01:04:34.290
Cynthia.
是辛西娅。

1251
01:04:35.190 --> 01:04:35.750
Cynthia!
辛西娅！

1252
01:04:36.970 --> 01:04:39.670
Played by Algerita Wynne-Lewis.
由阿尔杰丽塔·韦恩-刘易斯饰演。

1253
01:04:40.330 --> 01:04:41.750
This is a bit scandalous.
这有点轰动性。

1254
01:04:42.050 --> 01:04:45.050
I'm surprised Angela didn't have something to say about this.
我很惊讶安吉拉对此居然没什么好说的。

1255
01:04:45.410 --> 01:04:48.890
Angela was consumed with the fact that Pam was getting married while pregnant.
安吉拉的心思全在帕姆带球结婚这件事上。

1256
01:04:49.090 --> 01:04:50.810
She could barely focus on anything else.
她几乎无法专注于其他任何事情。

1257
01:04:51.270 --> 01:04:52.030
That's right.
没错。

1258
01:04:52.190 --> 01:04:54.890
She was focusing all her shame in that one direction.
她把所有的羞耻感都倾注在那一个方向上了。

1259
01:04:56.170 --> 01:05:05.330
I love that Michael goes up to Jim and Pam and asks when is he making his speech and says, because he'd like to go third to bat cleanup.
我喜欢迈克尔走向吉姆和帕姆，问他什么时候发表演讲，还说因为他想排在第四个出场打清垒。

1260
01:05:06.070 --> 01:05:06.350
Yeah.
是啊。

1261
01:05:06.730 --> 01:05:09.690
This is where we are going to meet Jim's parents for the first time.
我们在这里将第一次见到吉姆的父母。

1262
01:05:09.690 --> 01:05:18.530
We have Betsy Halpert, played by Perry Smith, and Gerald Halpert, played by Robert Pine, who is the father of actor Chris Pine.
贝茜·哈尔珀特由佩里·史密斯饰演，杰拉尔德·哈尔珀特由罗伯特·派恩饰演，他是演员克里斯·派恩的父亲。

1263
01:05:19.170 --> 01:05:20.430
People were so excited.
大家当时可兴奋了。

1264
01:05:20.990 --> 01:05:22.510
We were a little bit excited.
我们其实也有一点兴奋。

1265
01:05:23.030 --> 01:05:26.270
First of all, he's a lovely, lovely person and was so nice to everyone.
首先，他是一个非常非常可爱的人，对每个人都很好。

1266
01:05:26.330 --> 01:05:29.410
But there were a few folks excited that Chris Pine's dad was there.
但确实有些人因为克里斯·派恩的父亲在现场而感到激动。

1267
01:05:29.410 --> 01:05:30.470
It's true.
千真万确。

1268
01:05:30.770 --> 01:05:30.890
It's true.
确实如此。

1269
01:05:30.890 --> 01:05:34.670
Even though Robert Pine is like an incredibly successful actor in his own record.
尽管罗伯特·派恩本身就是一位极其成功的演员。

1270
01:05:34.670 --> 01:05:35.630
I know.
我知道。

1271
01:05:37.270 --> 01:05:42.790
Well, listen, Pam and Jim are pointing out Mima to Jim's parents.
好了，听着，帕姆和吉姆正在向吉姆的父母指出米玛的位置。

1272
01:05:42.790 --> 01:05:47.550
And she says, Mima is the woman in teal talking to my mom.
她说道，米玛就是那个穿着青绿色衣服、正在和我妈妈说话的女人。

1273
01:05:48.010 --> 01:05:55.230
Now, that was confusing to some viewers because, you know, we met Pam's mom in the sexual harassment episode in season two.
这让一些观众感到困惑，因为你知道的，我们在第二季的性骚扰那一集中见过帕姆的妈妈。

1274
01:05:55.810 --> 01:06:01.630
And the woman that we met as Pam's mom was not standing over by the woman in teal.
而我们之前见过的那个帕姆的妈妈，当时并没有站在那个穿青绿色衣服的女人旁边。

1275
01:06:01.990 --> 01:06:06.210
Because in this episode, Pam has a new mom.
因为在这集里，帕姆换了个新妈妈。

1276
01:06:06.430 --> 01:06:09.890
We had to cast a new actress as Pam's mom.
我们不得不重新选角扮演帕姆的妈妈。

1277
01:06:09.890 --> 01:06:10.490
Yeah.
是啊。

1278
01:06:11.450 --> 01:06:15.150
The original actress who played Pam's mom was Shannon Cochran.
原来扮演帕姆妈妈的女演员是香农·科克兰。

1279
01:06:15.710 --> 01:06:18.850
She was on tour doing a play.
她当时正在外地巡演一部话剧。

1280
01:06:19.070 --> 01:06:20.710
She was doing August Osage County.
她当时在演《八月：奥色治郡》。

1281
01:06:20.910 --> 01:06:23.130
And we could not get her for this episode.
我们无法请她来参演这一集。

1282
01:06:23.850 --> 01:06:25.250
Randy actually talked about this.
兰迪其实谈到过这件事。

1283
01:06:25.370 --> 01:06:32.890
He said this was a really difficult episode to schedule because we had so many different guest stars,
他说这一集的档期安排非常困难，因为我们有太多不同的客串演员了，

1284
01:06:33.110 --> 01:06:35.910
many of whom we had established in previous episodes.
其中许多人在之前的剧集里就已经出现过。

1285
01:06:35.910 --> 01:06:37.510
We had to get the same people.
我们必须请到原班人马。

1286
01:06:38.330 --> 01:06:40.810
We even had to shoot on two Saturdays.
我们甚至连续两个周六都在拍摄。

1287
01:06:40.930 --> 01:06:42.190
I don't know if you remember that, Angela.
安吉拉，我不知道你还记不记得。

1288
01:06:42.490 --> 01:06:49.230
But in order to get everybody in the same room together for the wedding part, we actually shot on Saturdays.
但为了让所有人都聚在同一个房间里拍摄婚礼部分，我们实际上是在周六进行拍摄的。

1289
01:06:49.410 --> 01:06:51.310
The one person we couldn't get was Shannon.
我们惟独没能请到的演员就是香农。

1290
01:06:51.990 --> 01:06:53.690
The writers talked about this.
编剧们讨论过这件事。

1291
01:06:54.210 --> 01:06:57.050
They felt that we had to have Pam's mom at the wedding.
他们觉得帕姆的妈妈必须出席婚礼。

1292
01:06:57.250 --> 01:06:57.770
They did not.
他们可不想这样。

1293
01:06:57.970 --> 01:06:58.250
Of course.
当然啦。

1294
01:06:58.750 --> 01:07:00.430
Like, Pam could get married without her mom.
比如，帕姆怎么可能在没有妈妈的情况下结婚呢。

1295
01:07:00.430 --> 01:07:06.670
No, they did not want to manufacture some kind of drama like that Pam's mom didn't come.
不，他们不想人为制造出诸如帕姆妈妈没来之类的情节戏剧。

1296
01:07:06.950 --> 01:07:07.450
Right.
没错。

1297
01:07:07.770 --> 01:07:13.630
Plus, they really wanted to introduce that storyline between Michael and Pam's mom.
另外，他们真的很想引入迈克尔和帕姆妈妈之间的那条故事线。

1298
01:07:14.630 --> 01:07:17.670
And that was an important storyline for this season.
那是本季一条非常重要的故事线。

1299
01:07:17.910 --> 01:07:22.970
And it looked like Shannon's tour schedule was going to bump into that as well.
而且看起来香农的巡演日程也会与此冲突。

1300
01:07:23.150 --> 01:07:26.450
So they made the decision to recast the role.
所以他们做出了重新选角的决定。

1301
01:07:26.890 --> 01:07:29.290
Pam's new mom was played by Linda Pearl.
潘的新妈妈由琳达·珀尔扮演。

1302
01:07:29.290 --> 01:07:32.610
When I met her, I was really struck with how alike we look.
我第一次见到她时，真的很惊讶我们长得这么像。

1303
01:07:32.750 --> 01:07:37.810
It's funny because the original actress, Shannon, kind of looks like my real mom.
很有意思的是，原本的演员香农长得有点像我的亲生妈妈。

1304
01:07:37.970 --> 01:07:41.030
But I thought Linda looked kind of like me.
但我觉得琳达长得有点像我。

1305
01:07:41.250 --> 01:07:44.370
I actually thought she looked like she could be my big sister.
我甚至觉得她长得可以当我姐姐。

1306
01:07:45.230 --> 01:07:47.150
And we were doing the math.
然后我们算了一下。

1307
01:07:47.150 --> 01:07:51.070
And we were like, wait, actually, like, we're not that far apart in age.
我们当时就想，等等，其实我们俩年龄差得并不算太大。

1308
01:07:51.170 --> 01:07:53.630
Like, she would have been 19 when she had me.
也就是说，她生我的那会儿应该才19岁。

1309
01:07:53.910 --> 01:07:55.590
A little bit of Hollywood magic there.
这里面有点好莱坞的魔力。

1310
01:07:55.770 --> 01:07:56.450
A little fudging.
稍微含糊了一下。

1311
01:07:56.450 --> 01:07:58.910
They tried to play it up with, like, her hair, makeup, wardrobe.
他们试图通过她的发型、妆容和服装来强化这种感觉。

1312
01:07:59.230 --> 01:08:00.730
But here's something crazy.
但有个疯狂的事实。

1313
01:08:00.790 --> 01:08:02.470
She's been acting for forever.
她演戏演了超级久。

1314
01:08:02.830 --> 01:08:04.670
She had been on Happy Days.
她曾出演过《欢乐时光》。

1315
01:08:04.930 --> 01:08:06.290
How cool is that?
这多酷啊？

1316
01:08:06.750 --> 01:08:07.850
Isn't that crazy?
是不是很疯狂？

1317
01:08:08.430 --> 01:08:09.870
Well, Linda was delightful.
总之，琳达非常讨人喜欢。

1318
01:08:10.150 --> 01:08:12.170
I loved getting to work with her.
我特别喜欢和她合作。

1319
01:08:12.530 --> 01:08:18.290
At 11 minutes, 3 seconds, people are making their way into where the rehearsal dinner is.
在11分3秒的时候，大家正朝着彩排晚宴的场地走去。

1320
01:08:18.290 --> 01:08:21.750
There is a sign that says Beasley Halpert.
那里有一个写着“比斯利·哈尔珀特”的牌子。

1321
01:08:22.910 --> 01:08:24.610
Now, Halpert is spelled wrong.
现在，哈尔珀特这个姓氏拼错了。

1322
01:08:24.990 --> 01:08:29.990
And some people on the internet at the time were like, oh, my gosh, they spelled Jim's last name wrong.
当时网上有些人就说，天哪，他们把吉姆的姓给拼错了。

1323
01:08:30.750 --> 01:08:32.930
Veda shared on the commentary, that was intentional.
维达在评论音轨中分享过，那是故意的。

1324
01:08:33.290 --> 01:08:39.430
That was like a little joke, a little hidden Jim, a little nugget, you know, that the hotel staff had spilled his name wrong.
那就像是一个小笑话，一个藏给吉姆的小彩蛋，你知道的，意思是酒店工作人员把他的名字拼错了。

1325
01:08:39.610 --> 01:08:41.130
So that was meant to be, you guys.
所以各位，那绝对是故意的。

1326
01:08:41.130 --> 01:08:49.090
Yes, Angela, on that little sign that I mentioned earlier, every time it's supposed to say Halpert, it says Halpert.
没错，安吉拉，正如我刚才提到的那个小牌子上写的，每次该出现“哈尔珀特”的地方，它都拼成了“Halpert”。

1327
01:08:49.390 --> 01:08:50.750
It's like a running joke.
这就像是一个贯穿始终的梗。

1328
01:08:50.850 --> 01:08:52.270
You can find many Halperts.
你能找到好几个“Halpert”。

1329
01:08:52.510 --> 01:08:56.250
The other information on the sign reads like this.
牌子上的其他信息是这样的。

1330
01:08:56.510 --> 01:09:00.450
Wedding rehearsal dinner, 7 to 8.40 p.m.
婚礼彩排晚宴，晚上7点到8点40。

1331
01:09:00.450 --> 01:09:02.590
Yeah, guys, you've got to get out.
对啊，各位，你们得离开。

1332
01:09:02.690 --> 01:09:03.390
Got to get out.
必须得走。

1333
01:09:03.670 --> 01:09:04.890
8.40, you're out.
8点40分，你们就得清场。

1334
01:09:04.970 --> 01:09:06.090
You have an hour and 40 minutes.
你们只有一个小时四十分钟。

1335
01:09:06.330 --> 01:09:08.050
Eat up, make your toast, get out the door.
赶紧吃完，致好祝酒词，然后出门。

1336
01:09:08.210 --> 01:09:11.850
And it is taking place in the Passion Package Room.
而且这个活动是在“激情套餐包厢”举行的。

1337
01:09:12.390 --> 01:09:12.830
Wow.
哇。

1338
01:09:13.730 --> 01:09:21.770
I can tell you that we filmed all of these rehearsal dinner scenes at the famous Smokehouse restaurant in Burbank.
我可以告诉大家，我们所有这些彩排晚宴的戏份都是在伯班克著名的烟屋餐厅拍摄的。

1339
01:09:22.390 --> 01:09:28.190
I don't know if you remember, Angela, but at the time, I lived in walking distance from the Smokehouse.
安吉拉，我不知道你还记不记得，当时我走路就能到烟屋餐厅。

1340
01:09:28.190 --> 01:09:31.050
Oh, you were so excited when we were filming there.
哦，我们去那儿拍戏时你可兴奋了。

1341
01:09:31.330 --> 01:09:34.050
I would walk home for lunch and I'd have lunch with Lee.
我会走回家吃午饭，然后和李一起吃午餐。

1342
01:09:34.870 --> 01:09:36.090
It was so great.
那感觉太棒了。

1343
01:09:36.950 --> 01:09:40.250
And guys, listen, the Smokehouse is a very famous restaurant.
而且大家听着，烟屋餐厅是一家非常著名的餐厅。

1344
01:09:40.470 --> 01:09:42.970
It is right across the street from Warner Brothers Studios.
它就在华纳兄弟制片厂的马路对面。

1345
01:09:43.370 --> 01:09:47.570
So a lot of, like, movie executives and actors eat there.
所以很多电影高管和演员都会在那里吃饭。

1346
01:09:47.910 --> 01:09:53.730
I guess George Clooney even named his production company after the Smokehouse restaurant.
我听说乔治·克鲁尼甚至用烟屋餐厅的名字来命名他的制作公司。

1347
01:09:54.010 --> 01:09:57.710
Yeah, because he filmed on the Warner Brothers lot and he would walk over there.
对，因为他曾在华纳兄弟的片场拍戏，而且他会步行去那里。

1348
01:09:57.710 --> 01:09:59.750
That's the Hollywood lore, anyway.
不管怎样，好莱坞流传的传说就是这样。

1349
01:10:00.130 --> 01:10:03.870
Well, the original Smokehouse only seated 46 people.
嗯，最初的烟屋餐厅只能容纳46人。

1350
01:10:04.370 --> 01:10:11.590
I found a whole little video documentary about it and I thought we should listen to a little audio clip about its history.
我找到了一部关于它的完整小纪录片，我觉得我们应该听一听关于它历史的一小段音频。

1351
01:10:11.810 --> 01:10:12.270
Great.
太棒了。

1352
01:10:13.390 --> 01:10:21.910
The original Smokehouse was started here at Riverside and Pass in Burbank in 1946 by two Lockheed engineers, Jim Stockton and Jack Monroe.
最初的“烟熏屋”餐厅于1946年由两位洛克希德公司的工程师吉姆·斯托克顿和杰克·门罗在伯班克的河滨路和帕斯路交汇处创立。

1353
01:10:22.450 --> 01:10:25.330
Jim was the promoter and front man and Jack was the cook.
吉姆负责宣传和出面交际，杰克则负责烹饪。

1354
01:10:26.010 --> 01:10:30.330
Opening night was attended by such neighborhood luminaries as Bob Hope and Bing Crosby.
开业当晚，鲍勃·霍珀和平·克罗斯比等邻近的名流都光临了。

1355
01:10:30.870 --> 01:10:36.610
Soon after, all 46 seats were regularly filled to capacity and it was time to look for larger quarters.
不久之后，所有46个座位就经常座无虚席，是时候寻找更大的地方了。

1356
01:10:36.610 --> 01:10:45.550
As fate would have it, the Red Coach Inn, built by Danny Kaye but never opened, was available and in 1948 became the permanent home of the Smokehouse.
命运弄人，由丹尼·凯伊建造却从未开业的红马车旅馆恰好空了出来，并于1948年成为了烟熏屋的永久址。

1357
01:10:45.770 --> 01:10:49.490
By 1952, Jim's younger brother Stan was running the restaurant.
到1952年，吉姆的弟弟斯坦已经开始经营这家餐厅了。

1358
01:10:49.690 --> 01:10:50.830
And Chef John L.
而厨师约翰·L·

1359
01:10:50.930 --> 01:10:56.950
Sullivan's unique recipe for garlic bread made the Smokehouse the largest purveyor of French bread west of the Mississippi.
沙利文独创的大蒜面包秘方，让烟熏屋成为了密西西比河以西最大的法式面包供应商。

1360
01:10:56.950 --> 01:11:01.550
Yeah, like their garlic bread was like the thing.
对啊，他们的蒜香面包简直就是招牌。

1361
01:11:01.790 --> 01:11:02.810
It's still the thing.
现在依然是招牌。

1362
01:11:03.250 --> 01:11:05.310
It brought in all the celebs.
这吸引了所有的名流。

1363
01:11:05.710 --> 01:11:09.930
I guess the new location could seat like 500 people.
我猜新店址大概能容纳500人左右。

1364
01:11:10.550 --> 01:11:13.590
Here's a list of the people that would go to the Smokehouse for this bread.
这里有一份为了这面包而去烟熏屋的名人名单。

1365
01:11:14.210 --> 01:11:17.910
Errol Flynn, Judy Garland, Robert Redford.
埃罗尔·弗林、朱迪·加兰、罗伯特·雷德福。

1366
01:11:18.330 --> 01:11:24.070
But the Smokehouse was known for respecting the privacy of celebrities.
但烟熏屋以尊重名人隐私而闻名。

1367
01:11:24.070 --> 01:11:26.370
They would never sell a story to the tabloids.
他们绝不会向小报出售八卦。

1368
01:11:27.070 --> 01:11:29.970
And when I first moved to Los Angeles, Angela,
安吉拉，当我刚搬到洛杉矶时，

1369
01:11:30.250 --> 01:11:40.590
I had a friend who told me that once a week they would go eat lunch at the Smokehouse to try to get discovered by executives who were coming there for lunch.
我有个朋友告诉我，他们每周去烟熏屋吃一次午餐，试图被那些来这里吃午餐的高管们发掘。

1370
01:11:41.050 --> 01:11:42.150
It never happened.
这从未发生过。

1371
01:11:42.310 --> 01:11:44.750
They never got discovered.
他们从来没有被发掘过。

1372
01:11:45.090 --> 01:11:49.130
I just want that guy in the ad to do something for office ladies.
我只希望广告里的那个家伙能为办公室女郎们做点什么。

1373
01:11:49.670 --> 01:11:50.510
Two gals.
两个女孩。

1374
01:11:50.850 --> 01:11:51.570
Angela Finsley.
安吉拉·芬斯利。

1375
01:11:51.950 --> 01:11:52.670
Jenna Fisher.
珍娜·费舍。

1376
01:11:52.990 --> 01:11:53.730
Sam Kiefer.
萨姆·基弗。

1377
01:11:54.090 --> 01:11:54.970
Cassie Jerkins.
卡西·杰金斯。

1378
01:11:55.130 --> 01:11:55.790
Sitting around.
坐在一起。

1379
01:11:56.030 --> 01:11:57.270
Talking about TV.
聊着电视节目。

1380
01:12:01.430 --> 01:12:05.690
You get a sense of like the mood of the Smokehouse when you listen to that.
当你听到这些时，你能感受到烟熏屋的那种氛围。

1381
01:12:05.870 --> 01:12:06.490
For sure.
确实。

1382
01:12:07.270 --> 01:12:09.310
Well, I think we should take a break.
好吧，我想我们该休息一下了。

1383
01:12:09.450 --> 01:12:12.650
And when we come back, Dwight is going to hold court at the kids table.
等我们回来后，德怀特将在儿童桌旁大放厥词。

1384
01:12:12.970 --> 01:12:15.070
And we're going to meet Pam's sister?
而且我们要见帕姆的妹妹吗？

1385
01:12:15.710 --> 01:12:16.330
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

1386
01:12:16.330 --> 01:12:16.530
What?
什么？

1387
01:12:16.710 --> 01:12:19.330
Pam has had a sister this whole time?
帕姆一直有个妹妹？

1388
01:12:19.750 --> 01:12:20.310
Yeah.
对啊。

1389
01:12:20.450 --> 01:12:22.390
And she's like a famous actress.
而且她就像个著名的女演员。

1390
01:12:23.150 --> 01:12:24.150
We'll be back.
我们马上回来。

1391
01:12:33.800 --> 01:12:34.960
We are back.
我们回来了。

1392
01:12:34.960 --> 01:12:38.080
And I can't wait because we're about to talk to Meemaw.
我等不及了，因为我们马上要和“奶奶”聊聊。

1393
01:12:38.660 --> 01:12:39.220
Aw.
哦。

1394
01:12:39.900 --> 01:12:40.460
Yes.
是的。

1395
01:12:41.480 --> 01:12:45.140
Meemaw, played by the amazing Peggy Stewart.
“奶奶”由演技精湛的佩吉·斯图尔特饰演。

1396
01:12:46.140 --> 01:12:55.120
First of all, I just want to say that I loved the detail that Meemaw had her napkin tucked into her blouse like a bib.
首先，我只想说我很喜欢“奶奶”把餐巾塞进衬衫领口像个围嘴一样的细节。

1397
01:12:55.380 --> 01:12:56.740
Did you notice this?
你注意到了吗？

1398
01:12:56.960 --> 01:12:57.600
I did.
我注意到了。

1399
01:12:57.600 --> 01:12:59.220
She wasn't going to mess up her outfit.
她可不想弄脏自己的衣服。

1400
01:12:59.500 --> 01:13:00.520
No, she was not.
不，她才不想呢。

1401
01:13:00.780 --> 01:13:05.180
I bet she also has a little rain bonnet for her hair.
我敢打赌她头上还戴着一顶防雨小凉帽。

1402
01:13:05.700 --> 01:13:10.700
My grandma had one of those because, you know, she would go get her hair done once a week at the salon.
我奶奶就有一个，因为，你知道的，她每周都会去美发沙龙做一次发型。

1403
01:13:11.040 --> 01:13:12.660
And they'd tease it all up.
然后他们会把头发弄得蓬松高耸。

1404
01:13:12.980 --> 01:13:14.300
Angela Martin had one.
安吉拉·马丁就有一个。

1405
01:13:15.100 --> 01:13:22.280
Meemaw says that Pam marrying Jim might just be restoring her faith in that side of the family.
米玛说，帕姆嫁给吉姆可能正在恢复她对那一大家子的信心。

1406
01:13:23.160 --> 01:13:27.100
And Pam's kind of like, oh, thanks, Meemaw.
而帕姆大概的反应是，哦，谢谢你，米玛。

1407
01:13:27.260 --> 01:13:29.700
I mean, nobody's perfect, but, you know.
我的意思是，人无完人，不过，你懂的。

1408
01:13:30.000 --> 01:13:34.120
And then Meemaw says she wouldn't care to live if she thought that was true.
然后米玛说，如果她觉得那是真的，她都不想活了。

1409
01:13:34.940 --> 01:13:36.480
Pam's Meemaw is Angela.
帕姆的米玛就是安吉拉。

1410
01:13:36.780 --> 01:13:37.660
I know.
我知道。

1411
01:13:40.460 --> 01:13:47.280
You know, when we were talking to Greg, Greg mentioned that Peggy Stewart, who played Meemaw, was in a whole bunch of Westerns.
你知道的，当我们和格雷格交谈时，格雷格提到扮演米玛的佩吉·斯图尔特参演过一大堆西部片。

1412
01:13:47.620 --> 01:13:52.060
But I mean, like, I can't even tell you how many she was in.
但我的意思是，简直数不清她演过多少部。

1413
01:13:52.060 --> 01:14:00.660
Just from 1944 to 1951, just for that seven years, she was in 35 Westerns.
光是从1944年到1951年，仅仅这七年里，她就演了35部西部片。

1414
01:14:00.740 --> 01:14:02.080
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

1415
01:14:02.460 --> 01:14:03.520
In seven years.
在七年里。

1416
01:14:03.720 --> 01:14:04.080
Yeah.
是啊。

1417
01:14:04.340 --> 01:14:07.360
She also has a ton of television credits.
她还有海量的电视剧作品。

1418
01:14:07.360 --> 01:14:10.080
Like, she was on Gunsmoke for five years.
比如，她出演过五年《荒野大镖客》。

1419
01:14:10.080 --> 01:14:15.300
She's been on The A-Team, Days of Our Lives, Seinfeld, Frasier.
她上过《天龙特攻队》、《我们的日子》、《宋飞正传》、《欢乐一家亲》。

1420
01:14:15.740 --> 01:14:17.080
She died recently.
她最近去世了。

1421
01:14:17.080 --> 01:14:20.440
In 2019, she was 95 years old.
在2019年，享年95岁。

1422
01:14:21.400 --> 01:14:22.520
She was a delight.
她是一个令人开心的人。

1423
01:14:22.840 --> 01:14:23.820
She was amazing.
她太棒了。

1424
01:14:23.960 --> 01:14:25.080
Everyone loved her on set.
片场每个人都喜欢她。

1425
01:14:25.280 --> 01:14:28.680
She completely held her own with her scenes with Steve.
她在和史蒂夫的对手戏中完全能压得住阵脚。

1426
01:14:29.040 --> 01:14:30.680
Oh, don't even get me started.
哦，快别跟我提这个了。

1427
01:14:30.680 --> 01:14:31.860
I can't wait to get to those.
我已经迫不及待想看到那些部分了。

1428
01:14:31.920 --> 01:14:32.200
I know.
我知道。

1429
01:14:32.360 --> 01:14:32.780
I know.
我知道。

1430
01:14:33.040 --> 01:14:34.300
How lucky were we?
我们是多么幸运啊？

1431
01:14:35.380 --> 01:14:41.080
Next, Pam's going to run into her dad and his much younger new girlfriend, Christy Kelly.
接下来，帕姆会碰到她爸爸和比他年轻得多新女朋友克里斯蒂·凯利。

1432
01:14:41.960 --> 01:14:44.060
Pam's dad was played by Rick Overton.
帕姆的爸爸由里克·奥弗顿饰演。

1433
01:14:44.460 --> 01:14:50.180
Remember the last time we saw him, he was just down in the parking lot with just some off-camera
还记得我们上次见他时，他就在停车场里，只有一些画外

1434
01:14:50.180 --> 01:14:50.700
dialogue.
对白。

1435
01:14:50.820 --> 01:14:51.740
Here he is.
他在这儿。

1436
01:14:51.860 --> 01:14:52.380
He's back.
他回来了。

1437
01:14:52.540 --> 01:14:53.420
He was so fun.
他太有趣了。

1438
01:14:53.600 --> 01:14:54.400
He's back.
他回来了。

1439
01:14:54.580 --> 01:14:56.620
And then Dwight is at the kids' table.
然后德怀特坐在儿童桌旁。

1440
01:14:57.020 --> 01:14:57.900
He is.
确实如此。

1441
