01:37:21.420 --> 01:37:26.380
Now we're going to head on down to the bar, where everyone is kind of looking to have
现在我们要去酒吧了，婚礼前夜，每个人都在那里寻找

1877
01:37:26.380 --> 01:37:28.200
a good time the night before the wedding.
乐子。

1878
01:37:28.920 --> 01:37:33.200
We shot all these bar scenes in the bar of the Sportsman's Lodge.
我们是在体育俱乐部Lodge的酒吧里拍摄所有这些酒吧场景的。

1879
01:37:34.060 --> 01:37:37.820
Incidentally, we did a table read in the bar as well one day.
顺便说一句，有一天我们也在酒吧里进行了一次剧本围读。

1880
01:37:38.580 --> 01:37:41.080
We were just table reading all over this place.
我们简直在这个地方到处围读。

1881
01:37:41.260 --> 01:37:43.640
This was two weeks of wonky, crazy table reads.
那是连续两周古怪、疯狂的剧本围读。

1882
01:37:43.800 --> 01:37:44.800
It really was.
确实如此。

1883
01:37:44.920 --> 01:37:46.100
But they were really fun.
但它们真的很有趣。

1884
01:37:46.640 --> 01:37:48.660
And Pam wants to get in on this.
而帕姆也想参与其中。

1885
01:37:48.660 --> 01:37:50.820
She wants to go down to the bar, maybe.
她也想去酒吧看看。

1886
01:37:50.980 --> 01:37:56.340
She's going to leave her room wearing her very giant necklace and big hoop earrings and her
她离开房间时戴着她那条巨大的项链、大耳环和

1887
01:37:56.340 --> 01:37:57.340
bangle bracelets.
手镯。

1888
01:37:57.880 --> 01:38:00.100
But she's going to run into Angela.
但她会遇到安吉拉。

1889
01:38:00.520 --> 01:38:01.380
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

1890
01:38:02.080 --> 01:38:04.620
Meemaw's not the only fun stopper in town.
咪玛可不是镇上唯一的扫兴鬼。

1891
01:38:05.340 --> 01:38:06.420
Angela's here, too.
安吉拉也在这里。

1892
01:38:06.660 --> 01:38:13.060
At 21 minutes, 12 seconds, the hallway where this scene takes place was not a real hallway.
在21分12秒处，发生这个场景的走廊并不是一条真正的走廊。

1893
01:38:13.800 --> 01:38:15.940
I remember shooting this, Angela.
我记得我们拍这场戏时的情景，安吉拉。

1894
01:38:16.300 --> 01:38:18.140
Yes, it was a fakie hallway.
是的，那是一条假走廊。

1895
01:38:18.140 --> 01:38:22.040
It was a tiny nook, and we had to cheat it to look like a hallway.
那是一个很小的角落，我们不得不借位把它拍得像一条走廊。

1896
01:38:22.240 --> 01:38:24.380
And they told you and I to hug the wall.
他们告诉我和你要紧贴着墙壁。

1897
01:38:24.680 --> 01:38:29.620
So, like, if you watch the scene, we're standing super close to the wall the whole time.
所以，如果你看这个场景，我们全程都离墙壁超级近。

1898
01:38:29.780 --> 01:38:32.220
And there wasn't a lot of wiggle room.
而且没有多少腾挪的空间。

1899
01:38:32.300 --> 01:38:36.820
Like, we couldn't walk far in either direction because we ran out of wall.
比如，我们没法朝任何一个方向走太远，因为墙到头了。

1900
01:38:37.040 --> 01:38:37.320
Yeah.
是的。

1901
01:38:37.660 --> 01:38:40.980
Well, Angela's going to talk Pam out of going to the bar.
安吉拉打算劝说帕姆打消去酒吧的念头。

1902
01:38:41.620 --> 01:38:44.020
By offering to go with her to the bar.
通过主动提出陪她一起去酒吧。

1903
01:38:44.020 --> 01:38:48.360
And basically just chaperone her for the night with, like, a judgy sneer the whole time.
基本上就是整晚当她的监护人，脸上带着那种评判式的冷笑。

1904
01:38:48.380 --> 01:38:49.400
So, Pam's like, I'm out.
所以，帕姆就觉得，我不去了。

1905
01:38:50.020 --> 01:38:50.200
Yeah.
没错。

1906
01:38:50.980 --> 01:39:00.760
At 21 minutes, 34 seconds, we see the famous Howling at the Moon t-shirt that Dwight is going to wear to pick up the ladies.
在第21分34秒，我们看到了那件著名的“对月长啸”T恤，德怀特打算穿着它去泡妞。

1907
01:39:01.320 --> 01:39:01.600
Ow!
噢！

1908
01:39:03.800 --> 01:39:04.480
Yeah.
对。

1909
01:39:05.220 --> 01:39:08.860
Paul and Greg talked about Dwight's t-shirt in the commentary.
保罗和格雷格在随片评论里谈到了德怀特的T恤。

1910
01:39:09.400 --> 01:39:13.200
I guess our wardrobe department just bought it online.
我猜我们的服装部门就是从网上买的。

1911
01:39:13.500 --> 01:39:17.000
And you can still buy this exact t-shirt.
而且你现在还能买到这件一模一样的T恤。

1912
01:39:17.160 --> 01:39:17.920
It's on Amazon.
亚马逊上有卖。

1913
01:39:18.300 --> 01:39:18.860
What?
什么？

1914
01:39:19.480 --> 01:39:20.160
Yes.
是的。

1915
01:39:20.320 --> 01:39:21.900
But guess what else?
但你猜还有什么？

1916
01:39:21.900 --> 01:39:28.560
In May of 2009, someone wrote a customer review that went viral.
2009年5月，有人写了一篇爆红的客户评论。

1917
01:39:29.460 --> 01:39:32.680
Brian Govern gave the t-shirt five out of five stars.
布莱恩·戈文给这件T恤打了五星好评。

1918
01:39:33.060 --> 01:39:37.380
His pros were, fits my girthy frame, has wolves on it, attracts women.
他的优点是：适合我魁梧的身材，上面有狼，吸引女性。

1919
01:39:37.600 --> 01:39:41.820
Cons, only three wolves, could probably use a few more, on the guns.
缺点：只有三只狼，手臂上大概还能再多加几只。

1920
01:39:42.340 --> 01:39:44.680
Cannot see wolves when sitting when arms crossed.
坐着且双臂交叉时看不到狼。

1921
01:39:44.920 --> 01:39:47.360
Wolves would have been better if they glowed in the dark.
如果狼会夜光就更好了。

1922
01:39:47.360 --> 01:39:52.140
And 41,274 people found this review helpful.
有41,274人觉得这条评论很有用。

1923
01:39:52.680 --> 01:39:54.320
That is fascinating, Angela.
太神奇了，安吉拉。

1924
01:39:54.660 --> 01:40:01.220
I am particularly fascinated by the fact that this review came out before this t-shirt ever appeared on our episode.
我特别着迷于这样一个事实：这篇评论发表的时间竟然早于这件T恤在我们剧集里登场的时间。

1925
01:40:01.500 --> 01:40:02.180
I know.
我知道。

1926
01:40:02.700 --> 01:40:03.220
Wow.
哇。

1927
01:40:03.620 --> 01:40:04.380
Pretty amazing.
相当惊人。

1928
01:40:04.860 --> 01:40:07.180
Guys, you can have the wolf shirt.
伙计们，你们可以穿那件狼头T恤。

1929
01:40:07.400 --> 01:40:08.740
I kind of want one.
我有点想买一件。

1930
01:40:09.160 --> 01:40:09.880
I know.
我也是。

1931
01:40:09.960 --> 01:40:10.940
I was thinking that, too.
我刚才也这么想。

1932
01:40:11.060 --> 01:40:13.860
I was like, do I need the wolf shirt but on a mug?
我在想，我需不需要一件印有狼头图案的马克杯？

1933
01:40:14.560 --> 01:40:15.540
Maybe I do.
也许我需要吧。

1934
01:40:15.540 --> 01:40:20.180
Well, you know who doesn't seem to mind Dwight's howling-at-the-moon shirt?
好吧，你知道谁好像并不介意德怀特的对月长啸T恤吗？

1935
01:40:20.720 --> 01:40:21.320
Who?
谁？

1936
01:40:21.960 --> 01:40:23.280
Pam's friend, Isabel.
帕姆的朋友伊莎贝尔。

1937
01:40:23.720 --> 01:40:27.560
And she finds all of Dwight's chatter about his horses and farm.
她觉得德怀特关于他的马和农场的那些唠叨。

1938
01:40:27.860 --> 01:40:29.060
So interesting.
非常有趣。

1939
01:40:29.600 --> 01:40:30.200
Yeah.
是啊。

1940
01:40:30.480 --> 01:40:33.980
The fact that he has nine and three-quarter horses.
事实上他有九又四分之三匹马。

1941
01:40:34.680 --> 01:40:36.180
How is that possible?
这怎么可能？

1942
01:40:36.740 --> 01:40:37.960
He explains.
他解释了。

1943
01:40:38.840 --> 01:40:41.620
I invented a device called Burger on the Go.
我发明了一种叫“随身汉堡”的装置。

1944
01:40:41.880 --> 01:40:49.100
It allows you to obtain six regular-sized hamburgers or 12 sliders from a horse without killing the animal.
它能让你在不伤害动物的情况下，从一匹马身上获取六个正常大小的汉堡或十二个小汉堡。

1945
01:40:49.840 --> 01:40:51.300
George Foreman is still considering it.
乔治·福尔曼还在考虑中。

1946
01:40:51.780 --> 01:40:53.140
Sharper Image is still considering it.
锐步还在考虑中。

1947
01:40:53.220 --> 01:40:54.440
Skymall is still considering it.
天空商城还在考虑中。

1948
01:40:54.700 --> 01:40:56.140
Hamakushlema is still considering it.
Hamakushlema还在考虑中。

1949
01:40:57.760 --> 01:40:58.660
Sears said no.
西尔斯拒绝了。

1950
01:40:59.280 --> 01:41:05.700
Well, when Greg saw this scene in editing, he was like, wait, that was a list of alternates.
嗯，当格雷格在剪辑时看到这一幕，他说，等等，那只是一长串备选台词。

1951
01:41:05.960 --> 01:41:08.900
Greg meant for only one of these to be used.
格雷格原本只打算用其中一个。

1952
01:41:09.300 --> 01:41:12.560
Instead, because he wasn't there, they thought it was a liSt.
结果，因为他不在，他们以为这是一份列表。

1953
01:41:12.560 --> 01:41:14.760
So Dwight ends up saying all of them.
所以德怀特最后把它们全念了出来。

1954
01:41:14.880 --> 01:41:17.760
But then they actually ended up liking it, so they left them all in.
但后来他们其实挺喜欢的，所以就全留下了。

1955
01:41:17.980 --> 01:41:22.660
We're going to go to Andy's room next because the party is in full swing.
接下来我们要去安迪的房间，因为派对正开得火热。

1956
01:41:22.660 --> 01:41:28.900
I want to remind you, this is the honeymoon suite that Andy has for one night.
我想提醒大家，这是安迪只住一晚的蜜月套房。

1957
01:41:29.440 --> 01:41:41.360
And Randy Cordray shared with us that our set designers had originally designed this huge heart-shaped kind of like hot tub bathtub
兰迪·科德雷跟我们分享说，我们的布景设计师原本设计了一个巨大的心形浴缸，类似于那种按摩浴缸

1958
01:41:41.360 --> 01:41:46.920
that was going to be in the room as kind of like an homage to the honeymoon suite.
打算放在房间里，算是对蜜月套房的一种致敬。

1959
01:41:47.120 --> 01:41:49.180
Well, they had design meetings.
嗯，他们开过设计会议。

1960
01:41:49.180 --> 01:41:50.600
They made it.
他们把它做出来了。

1961
01:41:50.600 --> 01:41:55.880
They even had pitched the idea that that's where Michael sleeps because he doesn't have a room.
他们甚至还提出过一个想法，那就是迈克尔睡在那里面，因为他没有房间。

1962
01:41:56.040 --> 01:41:57.440
He sleeps in the heart tub.
他睡在心形浴缸里。

1963
01:41:57.900 --> 01:41:59.320
It was in the room.
它确实在房间里。

1964
01:41:59.700 --> 01:42:01.120
You never see it.
你根本看不到它。

1965
01:42:01.300 --> 01:42:03.080
It never made it on camera.
它从来没出现在镜头里。

1966
01:42:03.300 --> 01:42:04.300
It was huge.
它超级大。

1967
01:42:04.300 --> 01:42:05.820
And they built it in the corner.
而且他们把它建在角落里。

1968
01:42:06.040 --> 01:42:07.320
And you never see it.
结果你压根儿看不见。

1969
01:42:07.560 --> 01:42:08.040
No.
没错。

1970
01:42:08.500 --> 01:42:11.600
So there's this huge dance-off happening in this room.
所以这个房间里正在进行一场盛大的斗舞。

1971
01:42:12.040 --> 01:42:15.680
Andy and Meredith are kind of doing like a robot challenge.
安迪和梅雷迪思在进行某种机器人舞挑战。

1972
01:42:16.060 --> 01:42:17.420
Kelly's like, what else you got?
凯利一副“你还有什么本事”的表情。

1973
01:42:17.580 --> 01:42:20.080
Because, you know, Kelly and Andy have a history of a dance-off.
因为，你知道的，凯利和安迪以前有过斗舞的渊源。

1974
01:42:20.600 --> 01:42:21.720
Well, guess what?
好了，你猜怎么着？

1975
01:42:22.460 --> 01:42:26.620
Andy's going to do the splits and he's going to hurt himself.
安迪要劈叉了，而且他会弄伤自己。

1976
01:42:26.920 --> 01:42:28.300
He can't get back up, y'all.
各位，他站不起来了。

1977
01:42:29.440 --> 01:42:31.120
Because he hurt his TT.
因为他伤到了他的小弟弟。

1978
01:42:31.880 --> 01:42:32.120
Yeah.
没错。

1979
01:42:32.320 --> 01:42:34.080
His scrote got hurt.
他的蛋蛋受伤了。

1980
01:42:34.480 --> 01:42:35.340
He did.
千真万确。

1981
01:42:35.720 --> 01:42:43.340
You know, Paul shared that Ed pitched that he thought just the splits wouldn't do that much damage,
你知道的，保罗分享说埃德提出过，他觉得光是劈叉不会造成那么严重的伤害，

1982
01:42:43.340 --> 01:42:46.240
that Andy should have something in his pocket that he lands on.
安迪口袋里应该揣着个东西，好让他落地时压到。

1983
01:42:46.240 --> 01:42:47.920
Oh, that was a good idea.
哦，这主意真不错。

1984
01:42:48.340 --> 01:42:48.560
Yeah.
是啊。

1985
01:42:49.220 --> 01:42:53.060
Aaron and Kevin are going to carry Andy to Pam's door.
亚伦和凯文要把安迪抬到帕姆的门前。

1986
01:42:53.900 --> 01:42:55.780
Pam, the bride.
帕姆，新娘子。

1987
01:42:56.000 --> 01:42:57.340
She's the sober one.
她是那个保持清醒的人。

1988
01:42:57.640 --> 01:42:59.020
Everyone else has been partying.
其他人都一直在狂欢。

1989
01:42:59.020 --> 01:42:59.820
I get that.
我懂的。

1990
01:43:00.140 --> 01:43:03.720
I mean, it's, listen, it's horrible timing for Pam, no doubt about it.
我是说，听着，对帕姆来说这时间点太糟糕了，毫无疑问。

1991
01:43:04.260 --> 01:43:08.060
Well, she's got to drive Andy to the hospital.
好吧，她得开车送安迪去医院。

1992
01:43:08.720 --> 01:43:14.120
And that's how this episode ends, with that news on Pam's doorstep.
这一集就是这样结束的，伴随着这个消息传到了帕姆的家门口。

1993
01:43:15.040 --> 01:43:18.420
Listen, we had one fan question that I wanted to address.
听着，我们有一个粉丝提问我想解答一下。

1994
01:43:18.700 --> 01:43:19.300
Amy C.
来自北卡罗来纳州夏洛特的艾米·C.

1995
01:43:19.580 --> 01:43:21.640
from Charlotte, North Carolina said,
说道，

1996
01:43:21.920 --> 01:43:27.280
My kids, who are 9 and 11, noticed that Daryl wasn't at the wedding in Niagara.
我的孩子们，一个9岁一个11岁，注意到达里尔没有去尼亚加拉瀑布的婚礼。

1997
01:43:27.580 --> 01:43:29.040
Where was he?
他去哪儿了？

1998
01:43:29.640 --> 01:43:30.820
Great catch!
真是好眼力！

1999
01:43:31.540 --> 01:43:35.520
Amy, tell your kids we're very proud of them over here on Office, ladies.
艾米，告诉你的孩子们，我们在《办公室女士》播客这里为他们感到骄傲。

2000
01:43:35.520 --> 01:43:36.140
Yeah.
没错。

2001
01:43:36.520 --> 01:43:38.060
So here's what it was.
事情是这样的。

2002
01:43:38.220 --> 01:43:44.300
It was decided that since Daryl was a close friend of Pam's ex-fiancee, Roy,
大家决定，由于达里尔是潘的前未婚夫罗伊的密友，

2003
01:43:45.100 --> 01:43:51.800
Pam and Jim would not have invited anyone from the warehouse, including Daryl, to the wedding.
潘和吉姆本不打算邀请仓库的任何人参加婚礼，包括达里尔。

2004
01:43:52.340 --> 01:43:58.900
But I'm pretty sure the reason they had to come up with that idea is because Craig was in New Orleans
但我很确定，他们之所以会想出这个借口，是因为克雷格当时正在新奥尔良

2005
01:43:58.900 --> 01:44:00.500
filming a movie at this time.
拍摄一部电影。

2006
01:44:00.900 --> 01:44:03.100
Well, that's 100% why he's not there.
没错，这就是他没去那里的一百个百分之百的原因。

2007
01:44:04.400 --> 01:44:04.960
Yeah.
是啊。

2008
01:44:05.560 --> 01:44:08.780
You know, Jim and Daryl are going to become good friends,
你知道的，吉姆和达里尔后来成了好朋友，

2009
01:44:08.780 --> 01:44:13.960
and they're going to be part of an upstart business together, you know, in later seasons.
而且他们俩在后面的几季里还要一起合伙创业呢。

2010
01:44:14.220 --> 01:44:16.600
But right now, that hasn't happened yet.
但现在，这一切还没发生呢。

2011
01:44:16.880 --> 01:44:20.820
You know, right now, that's sort of like Pam's ex-world.
你知道的，现在这还是潘的旧世界。

2012
01:44:21.220 --> 01:44:21.680
Yeah.
是啊。

2013
01:44:22.120 --> 01:44:24.860
Well, that is Niagara Part 1, you guys.
好了，各位，这就是《尼亚加拉瀑布》上集。

2014
01:44:24.860 --> 01:44:26.940
We're ending with an injured scrotum.
我们以一个受伤的阴囊结束了这一集。

2015
01:44:27.040 --> 01:44:28.980
We'll be back next week.
我们下周再见。

2016
01:44:28.980 --> 01:44:31.660
Like, we have so much to talk about next week.
话说，我们下周还有好多事情要聊呢。

2017
01:44:31.800 --> 01:44:34.660
I mean, we haven't gotten to the ceremony.
我的意思是，我们还没讲到婚礼仪式呢。

2018
01:44:34.720 --> 01:44:37.140
We haven't gotten to the actual falls.
我们还没讲到真正的瀑布呢。

2019
01:44:38.200 --> 01:44:39.260
There's more to say.
还有更多内容要说。

2020
01:44:39.440 --> 01:44:40.980
We hope you guys have a great week.
我们希望大家能度过愉快的一周。

2021
01:44:41.120 --> 01:44:43.880
Thanks for listening and sending in your questions and your comments.
感谢大家的收听，以及发来的问题和评论。

2022
01:44:44.220 --> 01:44:47.180
Huge thank you to Greg Daniels for being our guest today.
非常感谢格雷格·丹尼尔斯今天能来做我们的嘉宾。

2023
01:44:47.180 --> 01:44:53.380
And another big thank you to Randy Cordray, who really helped us dissect the ins and outs
还要特别感谢兰迪·科德雷，他真的帮我们剖析了这一集的方方面面

2024
01:44:53.380 --> 01:44:55.840
